+# Design Excellence baseline
+
+Pack 1.4.0 at f4fb20a2655eaa37c5089c6d91455cb56a238229. Inspection by Codex. No new model A/B trial was run.
+
+The owner reports product 21 versus 19 of 28 and visual craft 23 versus 27 of 40 for the CRM comparison. These are supplied results, not independently reproduced findings.
+
+Observed source gaps:
+
+- SKILL.md requires ten stages, record updates and three options without a short planning budget.
+- stages/01-research.md mandates 5 to 10 searches for every new project.
+- stages/02-brainstorm.md requires three mechanisms and five scores even for a specified dashboard.
+- stages/06-design-system.md bans 12px spacing and fixes Inter plus Fraunces.
+- patterns/app-screens.md A4 requires a context rail. This can compete with table width; causality in the reported run is unverified.
+- stages/08-build.md protects copied blocks unless a test fails, while current tests do not measure the supplied craft defects.
+- stages/09-test-and-critique.md has a premium website rubric, but no equal app rubric or anchored reference score.
+- scripts/deal.mjs ranks script checks above rubric cards and does not guarantee app craft coverage.
+- scripts/check-ui.mjs lacks mid-word, column squeeze, raw null, required chart, scroll-hint and type hierarchy checks.
+
+Baseline verification retained from onboarding: source validation and 157 mutations passed; 61 regression methods passed. Four browser failures and three token-data errors were traced to unavailable pinned Chromium and HTTP 403 for the tokenizer asset. This is previous-instance evidence, not validation of the forthcoming changes.
+
+Visual protocol: create an authored CRM fixture with the same labeled sample content before and after, capture at 1280x800 and 390x844, inspect every PNG. These illustrate the written rules and checker behavior. They are not independent model builds or evidence that the upgrade wins an A/B test.
